# packages.list -- the default package set ("world") for the
# "Postern for postmarketOS -- community edition" flavor.
#
# HONESTY / UNBOOTED: community, NON-attestable tier. This is the intended flavor
# world; it has NOT been resolved/installed on a device. Signed (who published),
# not reproducible (what it was built from). This is NOT "Postern OS".
# See ../PUBLISHED.md (what is LIVE) and README.md (the flavor spec).
#
# This file documents the set; it is consumed two ways:
#   - the postern-flavor package `depends=` mirrors the "flavor" rows below;
#   - build/build.sh installs the `postern` meta, which pulls the "meta" rows.
# Lines are "pkgname  # source  # why". Blank lines and #comments ignored.

# --- Postern packages (LIVE in the R2 apk repo -- PUBLISHED.md) --------------
postern                 # R2 apk repo (meta)   # pulls wallet + apps + phosh + tor
postern-wallet          # R2 apk repo          # offline PQ wallet CLI (software keystore)
postern-apps            # R2 apk repo (noarch) # web app suite + first-run note

# --- Flavor package (this overlay -- scaffold, UNBUILT) ----------------------
postern-flavor          # this overlay         # owns the ../overlay rootfs: services, firewall, MOTD, phosh defaults, first-run

# --- Privacy / security (Alpine + pmaports) ----------------------------------
arti                    # Alpine community     # in-process/on-device Tor (Rust); verify pkg name/ABI on device
nftables                # Alpine main          # /sbin/nft for the default-deny firewall
xdg-utils               # Alpine main          # xdg-open for the app launchers (also a postern-apps dep)

# --- UI shell (pmaports) -----------------------------------------------------
postmarketos-ui-phosh   # pmaports             # default shell; the postern meta hard-deps it (see README.md 1)

# --- Notes -------------------------------------------------------------------
# * `tor` (C daemon) is currently pulled by the postern meta's depends; the
#   flavor documents the Arti (Rust) direction and ships the Arti overlay
#   wiring. Reconciling the meta's `tor` dep is flagged for the APKBUILD owners
#   (README.md 2), not changed here.
# * FDE unlock (unl0kr/osk-sdl) is chosen at pmbootstrap install time, not by a
#   package; verify the current v26.06 component name on device.
# * notify-send (libnotify) is optional -- the first-run helper degrades
#   gracefully without it.
